sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Admin
    box rgb(232,240,254) Layer 1 Presentation
        participant R as event_routes
    end
    box rgb(232,245,233) Layer 2 Application
        participant E as EventService
        participant AU as AuthService
    end
    box rgb(255,243,224) Layer 3 Data access and integration
        participant W as UnitOfWork
        participant ER as EventRepository
        participant M as EmailSender
    end
    box rgb(243,229,245) Layer 4 External systems
        participant DB as PostgreSQL
        participant SMTP as SMTP provider
    end

    A->>R: GET /admin/requests
    R->>E: list_pending_events(admin_id)
    E->>AU: require_role(admin_id, ADMIN)
    E->>ER: pending(before = None)
    ER->>DB: SELECT event WHERE status = pending ORDER BY start_time
    E-->>R: pending requests
    R-->>A: request list

    A->>R: POST /admin/requests/{id} (decision, reason)
    alt decision = approve
        R->>E: approve_event(event_id, admin_id)
    else decision = reject
        R->>E: reject_event(event_id, admin_id, reason)
    end
    E->>AU: require_role(admin_id, ADMIN)
    alt user is not an admin
        AU-->>E: raise PermissionDeniedError
        E-->>R: raise PermissionDeniedError
        R-->>A: 403 page
    else admin
        E->>W: begin()
        E->>ER: get_for_update(event_id)
        ER->>DB: SELECT event FOR UPDATE
        alt status is not PENDING, or reject with empty reason
            E->>W: rollback()
            E-->>R: raise ValidationError
            R-->>A: request list with error
        else approve
            E->>E: status = OPEN, reviewed_by, reviewed_at
            E->>ER: save(event)
            ER->>DB: UPDATE event
            E->>W: commit()
            E->>AU: get_user(organizer_id)
            E->>M: send_event_decision(email, title, approved = true)
            M->>SMTP: decision e-mail
            E-->>R: event
            R-->>A: 303 redirect to /admin/requests
        else reject
            E->>E: status = REJECTED, reviewed_by, reviewed_at, rejection_reason
            E->>ER: save(event)
            ER->>DB: UPDATE event
            E->>W: commit()
            E->>AU: get_user(organizer_id)
            E->>M: send_event_decision(email, title, approved = false, reason)
            M->>SMTP: decision e-mail
            E-->>R: event
            R-->>A: 303 redirect to /admin/requests
        end
    end
    Note over E,ER: active_on() ignores rejected events, so a rejected request frees its facility slot (UC-07). A scheduled job calls expire_pending_requests(now), which uses pending(before = now) and rejects them without a reviewer.
